{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `x`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `x` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, `x ~ poisson(theta .* t)`. The other data variables, `N` and `t`, are context inputs used as a size and exposure predictor. Each parameter (`alpha`, `beta`, and `theta`) has exactly one built-in prior before later use.
","model_safe_stan":"// BUGS pump example (Vol 1, Example 2)
data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0> x;
  vector[N] t;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> beta;
  vector<lower=0>[N] theta;
}
model {
  alpha ~ exponential(1.0);
  beta ~ gamma(0.1, 1.0);
  theta ~ gamma(alpha, beta);
  x ~ poisson(theta .* t);
}

","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"t":[1.0,2.0,3.0],"x":[1,2,4]}","protected_variables":["x"]}
